<title>GERMANY: Buba sets ERM bands against lira.</title>
<headline>Buba sets ERM bands against lira.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank said on Monday that it set intervention rates for the mark against the lira after its re-entry into the Exchange Rate Mechanism at 990 lire parity at 0.8699 marks per 1,000 lira to buy and 1.1729 marks per 1,000 lira to sell.</p>
<p>The German central bank also said the levels against other currencies in the ERM were unchanged.  </p>
<p>The Bundesbank gave the following intervention levels for other currencies in the ERM</p>
<p>    CURRENCY			  BUY	 SELL</p>
<p>    100 Belgian francs	    4.175     5.630</p>
<p>    100 Luxembourg francs	 4.175     5.630</p>
<p>    100 Danish krone		22.575    30.445</p>
<p>    100 French francs	     25.675    34.625</p>
<p>    1   Irish punt		  2.076     2.800</p>
<p>    100 Dutch guilder	     86.780    90.770</p>
<p>    100 Spanish peseta	    1.0123    1.13650</p>
<p>    100 Portuguese escudo	 0.8401    1.1328</p>
<p>    100 Austrian schilling	12.241    16.505</p>
<p>    100 Finnish marrka	    28.328    38.197</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
